<description>
Compress the stacked colored bars into a compact ordered table with the control pixel on the selected row.

Input structure
- A background grid contains several full-width colored bars from top to
  bottom; the last bar is the base/separator color.
- Each non-base bar may have an aligned three-column comb motif below it,
  alternating side-pair rows with solid rows.
- A singleton control pixel sits away from the colored motifs.

Rule
- Make one output row per non-base bar, preserving top-to-bottom order.
- In that row, paint the bar color once for each solid three-pixel row in
  its motif, then paint the base-bar color in the separator column.
- The singleton control pixel sits immediately above the base bar. Among
  motifs whose open side-pair parity is compatible with that bottom row,
  put the control pixel in the output row with the fewest solid rows; use
  horizontal distance to the motif center only to break count ties.

Key insight
- The vertical comb height is a count, while the control pixel is read by
  projecting it onto the center gap of compatible comb rows rather than by
  its vertical band alone.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "full-width colored bars with aligned three-column comb motifs; the final full-width bar is the separator color",
  "dst": "compact rows in the same top-to-bottom bar order",
  "transform": "paint each row with the bar color repeated once per solid motif row, append the separator color column, and place the singleton control pixel on the row whose open motif center is nearest to it",
  "multi_step": "top-to-bottom order breaks equal marker-center distances",
  "grid_shape": "one row per non-separator bar; columns are count slots plus separator and control-pixel columns"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 21 rows x 21 cols [observed]
  background: 0
  bars:
    count: 3 source bars + 1 base bar (last), all full-width solid-color rows
    colors: all distinct non-bg non-marker colors; base bar always color 9 [observed]
    spacing: regions between consecutive bars have height 3-7 rows
    first_bar: row 1-2; base_bar: row 19-20 (last or second-to-last row)
  motifs:
    structure: 3-col-wide comb below its bar; alternating side-pair / solid rows starting with side-pair
    height: 2*S+1 rows where S = solid_count (0-3); region may have extra empty rows after motif
    solid_count: 0-3 per motif (0 means no motif at all); determines output count for that row
    column: each motif placed at arbitrary column (left_col in 2..17), independently per motif
  marker:
    color: always 5 [observed]; exactly 1 pixel in the grid
    row: immediately above the base bar (base_bar_row - 1)
    clearance: not 8-adjacent to any non-base colored object; adjacency to the base bar below is allowed
    side_pair_alignment: (marker_row - bar_row) % 2 == 1 for at least one motif with center_col
    selection: among side-pair-aligned motifs with solid_count > 0, marker selects the motif with the fewest solid rows; if counts tie, select the motif whose center_col is closest to marker_col; top-to-bottom breaks remaining ties
  output:
    shape: N x (N+2) where N = number of source bars (3 in all examples)
    row_i: first S cells = bar_i color, rest bg; col N = base_bar color; col N+1 = marker if selected

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick N=3 source bar colors + base color (9) + marker color (5), all distinct non-zero.
    2. Pick solid counts S_i for each source bar (each 0-3).
    3. Build output grid (N x N+2) from solid counts and bar colors.
    4. Assign marker to one output row by the bottom-control rule; set that row's last col = 5.
    5. Compute required region heights: max(2*S_i+1, 3) per source bar, plus base-bar region >= 2*max_compatible_offset+1.
    6. Lay out bars top-to-bottom on 21-row grid: row 0 = bg, bar rows with motif regions between them, base bar near bottom.
    7. Place each motif's 3-col comb at a random column in the region below its bar.
    8. Place marker pixel immediately above the base bar, in a cell not 8-adjacent
       to any non-base colored object.
       Choose the target from bottom-row side-pair-aligned motifs with the minimum solid_count;
       if several have the same count, make the target closest to the marker column.
    9. Verify solver reproduces the intended output.
```
